 -ed, -s, -er, -est) yield INFLECTION-MATCH; derivational suffixes (-ness, -ment, -tion/-sion, -ity, -ance/-ence, -ledge, -al, -age, -acy, -hood, -ship) yield NOMINALIZATION-EXTENSION; empirical cross-check (-ance: 'resemblance' Bundle 2 D.2 verb→noun anchor; -acy: 'accuracy' Bundle 2 D.2 adj→noun anchor; -ledge: 'knowledge' dev-24 SKIP cross-check); TEST (c) -ing borderline disambiguation — DEFAULT INFLECTION-MATCH (conservative; -ing has stronger inflectional tradition for gerund/participle than for deverbal nominalization in English); EXCEPTION (i) NOMINALIZATION-EXTENSION when claim-text syntactic context disambiguates toward deverbal-noun usage (determiner+head construction "the knowing of X"; adjective+noun construction "intuitive knowing"; possessive+noun construction "his knowing"); EXCEPTION (ii) NOMINALIZATION-EXTENSION when ontology metadata distinguishes node as deverbal-noun. EMPIRICAL ANCHOR n=1 (dev-24 'knowing' borderline; sufficient for principle-codification per line 658 single-dispositive-case + §5.4.2 negative-boundary-codification precedents): claim-aristotle-da-3.3-066 (dev-24) — TEST (a) word-class polysemy verb-form/noun-form; TEST (b) -ing canonically inflectional; TEST (c) -ing borderline DEFAULT INFLECTION-MATCH applies (claim-text syntactic context surfaces 'knowing' in argumentative-mode predicate context without deverbal-noun marker); 'knowing' classifies as INFLECTION-MATCH; cross-word fire NOT triggered per §3.4 D.3 cross-word framework (which operates on cross-word-class pairs); dev-24 SKIP disposition substantively correct under E.3 boundary criterion. dev-24 'knowledge' CROSS-CHECK DISPOSITION: TEST (a) word-class change verb→noun + TEST (b) -ledge derivational suffix → NOMINALIZATION-EXTENSION classification within Audi-031 broader scope per D.2; under E.3 + Audi-031 STANDING (post-Bundle 2 D.2 codification 2026-05-02) dev-24 'knowledge' would FIRE as Audi-031 verb→noun nominalization-extension (`knowledge` Aristotle primary-citat